│    18     URL-configured notification services, and for e-mail that means a                                                                                 │
│    19     mailto:// URL built from a host/port instead of a live socket, plus a                                                                             │
│    20     boolean success/failure return from .notify() instead of exceptions.                                                                              │
│    21                                                                                                                                                       │
│    22     This function builds a small first-party adapter (_AppriseSMTPClient)                                                                             │
│    23     that stores host/port, lazily imports apprise (mirroring the original                                                                             │
│    24     lazy `import smtplib` so the module can still be imported without the                                                                             │
│    25     dependency installed), and exposes a `.sendmail(sender, recipients,                                                                               │
│    26     message)` method so existing call sites do not need to change. The                                                                                │
│    27     wrapper parses the raw MIME-ish `message` string for the `Subject:`                                                                               │
│    28     header and the body below the blank line, then forwards them via                                                                                  │
│    29     apprise's `.notify(title=..., body=...)` to a mailto:// URL carrying                                                                              │
